  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Remnants**: back after 65 archived shows (2077 days); rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **Lucky to be Alive**: rare: 14 archived performances [4]\n- **banter: three beautiful nights**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Why Can't We Live Together**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2023-11-11.at943.engsky** (recommended): source not stated; 27 songs; 142 min [1]\n- **mmj2023-11-11.vwmule**: source not stated; 18 songs; 139 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [2]. Said about its sound: Reviewer describes the sound as clear, with little room reverb, from a mezzanine position [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- This was the third of three nights at the Chicago Theatre, with Devon Gilfillian opening [2]\n- Poster art for the run was by Guy Burwell and Clinton Reno [2]\n- Uploader considers this night's recording definitely better than the Thursday show's recording from the same run [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2023-11-11.at943.engsky**: taped by EnglishSkylarking; source: AT943/CMC-8 > R-07 [1]. Also: Recorded from right side near front of balcony with Audio-Technica AT943 mics into a Roland R-07 at 24-bit/88.2kHz, then edited and converted to 16-bit/44.1kHz FLAC [1]\n- **mmj2023-11-11.vwmule**: taped by Alex Leary; transferred by Alex Leary; source: Microtech Gefell M21 > nBob actives > Sound Devices MixPre-6 (24/48) [2]",
